@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Contact Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account contact information transfers properly to the account index.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Partner |
	| Updated Partner   |
	* I tear down the team roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Partner |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "A Liferay DXP Product" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| A Liferay DXP Product |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Platinum Subscription |
	* I tear down the external links for the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on koroneiki with the following entity id and domain values
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey}   | salesforce |
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey}   | dossiera   |
	| ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} | salesforce |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| A Liferay DXP Product  |
	| Platinum Subscription  |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products with their respective field values
	| A Liferay DXP Product | startDate | ${staticStartDate}       |
	| A Liferay DXP Product | startDate | ${staticFutureStartDate} |
	| Platinum Subscription | startDate | ${staticStartDate}       |
	| Platinum Subscription | startDate | ${staticFutureStartDate} |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Liferay DXP Product |
	| Platinum Subscription |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Account Customer Role |
	| Second Account Customer Role |
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korpro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Onepro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORPROKORPRO |
	| ONEPROONEPRO |

Scenario: View contact
	Testing the ability to create a contact in Dossiera and viewing the respective contact in the provisioning account details page

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message on sandbox with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Contact Role                           | Liferay Account Customer Role              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | A Liferay DXP Product                      |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I create a team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" for the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}"
	And I create a team role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the partner role |
	| Name        | Partner                  |
	| Type        | Account                  |
	And I assign the team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" on the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Koroneiki Partner"
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRO Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Liferay Account Customer Role        |
	| User Status   | UNVERIFIED                           |
	When I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	Then I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry in position number "3" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Assigned Contact > PRO Koroneiki1 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                      |
	| Update Field New Value      | Liferay Account Customer Role            |

Scenario: View verified contact
	Testing the ability to create a verified contact in Dossiera and viewing the respective contact in the provisioning account details page

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message on sandbox with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Contact Role                           | Liferay Account Customer Role              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | A Liferay DXP Product                      |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I create a team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" for the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}"
	And I create a team role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the partner role |
	| Name        | Partner                  |
	| Type        | Account                  |
	And I assign the team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" on the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Koroneiki Partner"
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I update a koroneiki contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values
	| Email Address Verified | true |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRO Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Liferay Account Customer Role        |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	When I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	Then I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

Scenario: View and search multiple contacts
	Testing the ability to create several contacts in Dossiera and koroneiki and viewing the respective contacts in the provisioning account details page

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message on sandbox with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Contact Role                           | Liferay Account Customer Role              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | A Liferay DXP Product                      |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I create a team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" for the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}"
	And I create a team role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the partner role |
	| Name        | Partner                  |
	| Type        | Account                  |
	And I assign the team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" on the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Koroneiki Partner"
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the second customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Second Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                              |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Second Account Customer Role |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRO Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Liferay Account Customer Role        |
	| User Status   | UNVERIFIED                           |
	And I should be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRO Koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Second Account Customer Role         |
	| User Status   | UNVERIFIED                           |
	When I search and filter the accounts details page using the following parameters
	| Keyword | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Filter  | Liferay Account Customer Role        |
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRO Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Liferay Account Customer Role        |
	| User Status   | UNVERIFIED                           |
	And I should not be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I clear the account details search
	And I search and filter the accounts details page using the following parameters
	| Keyword | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Filter  | Second Account Customer Role         |
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRO Koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Second Account Customer Role         |
	| User Status   | UNVERIFIED                           |
	And I should not be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I clear the account details search
	And I search and filter the accounts details page using the following parameters
	| Keyword | PRO                           |
	| Filter  | Liferay Account Customer Role |
	| Filter  | Second Account Customer Role  |
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRO Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Liferay Account Customer Role        |
	| User Status   | UNVERIFIED                           |
	And I should be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRO Koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Second Account Customer Role         |
	| User Status   | UNVERIFIED                           |
	When I remove the "Second Account Customer Role" search filter
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRO Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Liferay Account Customer Role        |
	| User Status   | UNVERIFIED                           |
	And I should not be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I remove the "Liferay Account Customer Role" search filter
	And I search and filter the accounts details page using the following parameters
	| Filter  | Second Account Customer Role |
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRO Koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Second Account Customer Role         |
	| User Status   | UNVERIFIED                           |
	And I should not be able to view the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	Then I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I search and filter the accounts details page using the following parameters
	| Keyword | PRO |
	Then I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry in position number "3" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Assigned Contact > PRO Koroneiki1 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                      |
	| Update Field New Value      | Liferay Account Customer Role            |
	And the history entry in position number "14" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Koroneiki Admin > Assigned Contact > PRO Koroneiki2 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                                        |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | Second Account Customer Role                        |

Scenario: View contact without additional role
